# Highlights

1. The green approach was developed to extract collagen using pepsin and ultra-sonication time from chicken sternal cartilage

2. The yield of ultrasound-treated PSC-II was significantly increased as compared to non-ultrasound-treated

3. Secondary structure collagen-II was partially altered with prolonged ultra-sonication time  4. Ultrasound-treated collagen-II showed superior functional properties and thermal stability  5. Utilization of ultrasound for extraction and expand the application of collagen-II at industrial level
